<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rada'a</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rada'a is a town in the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, in al-Bayda governorate, south-east of Sanaa. It was a home and capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirid dynasty</a>, which ruled much of Yemen from 1454 to 1517, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiriya-madrasa">Amiriya Madrasa</a>, completed in 1504, is one of the most celebrated monuments of Yemen. A citadel stands above the old town.</p></div>
